    "explanation": "1. CONCEPT:\nSurface gravity is proportional to mass and inversely proportional to the square of radius: $g = \\frac{G M}{R^2} \\implies \\frac{g_p}{g_e} = \\left(\\frac{M_p}{M_e}\\right) \\left(\\frac{R_e}{R_p}\\right)^2$.\n\n2. GIVEN:\nPlanet mass $M_p = 2 M_e$, planet radius $R_p = 2 R_e$.\n\n3. FORMULA / PRINCIPLE:\n\\frac{g_p}{g_e} = \\frac{M_p}{M_e} \\times \\left(\\frac{R_e}{R_p}\\right)^2 = \\frac{2}{2^2} = \\frac{2}{4}\n\n4. STEP-BY-STEP SOLUTION:\n1. Ratio of gravity: g_p / g_e = 2 / 4 = 0.5.\n2. Planet surface gravity: g_p = 0.5 * 9.8 = 4.90 m/s^2.\n\n5. FINAL ANSWER:\nOption A: 4.90 m/s^2\n\n6. QUICK TIP:\nRemember to square the radius in the denominator: (2)^2 = 4!",
