    "correctAnswer": "A",
    "correctIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "1. CONCEPT:\nFor apparent weightlessness at the equator, the apparent acceleration due to gravity must be zero: $g' = g - \\omega^2 R = 0 \\implies \\omega = \\sqrt{\\frac{g}{R}}$.\n\n2. GIVEN:\nGravity $g = 10\\text{ m/s}^2$, Earth radius $R = 6400\\text{ km} = 6.4 \\times 10^6\\text{ m}$.\n\n3. FORMULA / PRINCIPLE:\n\\omega = \\sqrt{\\frac{g}{R}}\n\n4. STEP-BY-STEP SOLUTION:\n1. $\\omega^2 = \\frac{10}{6.4 \\times 10^6} = \\frac{1}{640,000} = 1.5625 \\times 10^{-6}$.\n2. $\\omega = \\sqrt{1.5625 \\times 10^{-6}} = 1.25 \\times 10^{-3}\\text{ rad/s}$.\n3. This is approximately 17 times faster than Earth's present angular speed ($7.27 \\times 10^{-5}\\text{ rad/s}$).\n\n5. FINAL ANSWER:\nOption A: 1.25 x 10^-3 rad/s\n\n6. QUICK TIP:\nCondition for equator weightlessness: $\\omega = \\sqrt{g/R} \\approx 1.25 \\times 10^{-3}\\text{ rad/s}$. The day would then be only 84 minutes long!",
